#. type: Title #
#: README.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quarkus.io Website"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "はじめに"

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "These instructions will get you a copy of the Quarkus.io website up and running on your local machine for development and testing purposes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: README.md:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Java 21+\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maven (or use the included `./mvnw` wrapper — no separate Maven install required)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: README.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running locally"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Fork the [project repository](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkusio.github.io), then clone your fork:\n"
"    ```sh\n"
"    git clone git@github.com:YOUR_USER_NAME/quarkusio.github.io.git\n"
"    ```\n"
"2. Change into the project directory:\n"
"    ```sh\n"
"    cd quarkusio.github.io\n"
"    ```\n"
"3. Start the dev server:\n"
"    ```sh\n"
"    ./serve.sh\n"
"    ```\n"
"    This runs `mvn quarkus:dev` and serves the full site (including guides) at [http://localhost:8080](http://localhost:8080).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    For a faster startup without guides:\n"
"    ```sh\n"
"    ./serve-noguides.sh\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Or with only the latest guides (latest and main branches):\n"
"    ```sh\n"
"    ./serve-only-latest-guides.sh\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> [!NOTE]\n"
"> The startup process may take a minute or two on the first run while Maven downloads dependencies and Roq generates the site. Subsequent starts are faster. Once ready, you will see output like:\n"
">\n"
"> ```\n"
"> Listening on: http://0.0.0.0:8080\n"
"> ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid " If an error occurs mentioning a name conflict, try:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: README.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker compose up --force-recreate\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: README.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now browse to [http://localhost:4000](http://localhost:4000).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: README.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using a local Ruby environment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Jekyll static site generator docs](https://jekyllrb.com/docs/).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: README.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install a full [Ruby development environment](https://jekyllrb.com/docs/installation/). If you use `rvm`, run: `rvm use 3.2.3`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: README.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install [bundler](https://jekyllrb.com/docs/ruby-101/#bundler)  [gems](https://jekyllrb.com/docs/ruby-101/#gems)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: README.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "   gem install bundler\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: README.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fork the [project repository](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkusio.github.io), then clone your fork.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: README.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "   git clone git@github.com:YOUR_USER_NAME/quarkusio.github.io.git\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: README.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change into the project directory:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: README.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "   cd quarkusio.github.io\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: README.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use bundler to fetch all required gems in their respective versions\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: README.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "   bundle install\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#: README.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the site and make it available on a local server\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: README.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "   ./serve.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Or if you want it faster and okay to not have guides included use the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: README.md:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "   ./serve-noguides.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#: README.md:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now browse to http://localhost:4000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:86
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
">[!NOTE]\n"
">If you encounter any unexpected errors during the above, please refer to the [troubleshooting](https://jekyllrb.com/docs/troubleshooting/#configuration-problems) page or the [requirements](https://jekyllrb.com/docs/installation/#requirements) page, as you might be missing development headers or other prerequisites.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "**For more regarding the use of Jekyll, please refer to the [Jekyll Step by Step Tutorial](https://jekyllrb.com/docs/step-by-step/01-setup/).**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: README.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deploying to GitHub Pages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The website deployment is automatically performed by GitHub Actions (when commits are pushed to the `main` branch).\n"
"If for some reason you need to deploy from your local machine, follow these instructions:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: README.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the [act](https://github.com/nektos/act#installation) executable to run GitHub Actions locally\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: README.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `act -s GITHUB_TOKEN=<GITHUB_TOKEN>`, where *<GITHUB_TOKEN>* needs to be replaced with a token that allows you to push to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkusio.github.io repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: README.md:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing a blog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> [!WARNING]\n"
"> Using generative AI in *assisting* writing is fine, but please don't use it to write entire posts.\n"
"> Used badly, generative AI has a tendency to use complex words and phrasing. This makes the content hard to read and understand. Always review your blog with a human reader in mind, make sure it's factually correct and especially keep the human touch and opinions in the content.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: README.md:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "To write a blog:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "create an author entry in [_data/authors.yaml](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkusio.github.io/blob/main/_data/authors.yaml)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "`emailhash` you can get by running `echo -n your@email.org | md5sum` on Linux or `echo -n your@email.org | md5` on macOS using an email you have registered from the [Gravatar service](https://gravatar.com),\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "create a blog entry under [content/posts](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkusio.github.io/tree/main/content/posts)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "the file name is `yyyy-mm-dd-slug.adoc`. Set the `date` to the same value in the front matter.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`tags` should be used with some care as an archive page is created for each of them. Below are some basic rules to try to follow:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`quarkus-release` used for Quarkus release blogs\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`announcement` used for general announcements with some impact.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`extension` used for blogs related to a specific extension.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`user-story` used for stories from users/companies adopting Quarkus.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`development-tips` used for blogs with tips to develop using Quarkus or Quarkus itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "add a tech specific tag like `kafka` if your post has a significant mention/relevance to that technology.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "tags is a space-separated list: `tags: extension grpc`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "tags must be in lowercase\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "it's in asciidoc format, there is an example at [2019-06-05-quarkus-and-web-ui-development-mode.adoc](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkusio.github.io/blob/main/content/posts/2019-06-05-quarkus-and-web-ui-development-mode.adoc)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "Be aware that the `date` attribute in the front matter defines when the article will be published. Posts with a future date will not be visible in production until that date arrives; use `./serve.sh` locally to preview them regardless of date.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: README.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "send a pull request against the main branch and voilà\n"
msgstr ""

